{"request_sha256": "f78585c59ef7052ac86b2386964164c610cd3e17f35cdfa31cb6f0a3dd07cc10", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "f5bb29edb519503c2d2134a77cbf0aa8088b6091c95038568890c0a1a71946cd", "schema_sha256": "b11348cd1fb9f87dee1f7d8b64746455da08f64a4885c641943f00ea25a47f5f", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 5609}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["Crown fronds in both seeds are far too short and thin. Crown spread is only about a quarter of the visible trunk height, and the fronds are sparse spokes with tiny leaflets. The references show a massive crown of long, dense, plumose fronds (render-0, render-1, reference-0, reference-1).", "The crown is a radial starburst held mostly upward and outward. Only a few short fronds dip slightly below the crown apex. There is no heavy recurved, drooping lower tier like the one in reference-0 (render-0, render-1, render-2).", "The seed-1 trunk is wavy, with a visible S-bend in its upper third below the crown (render-0, render-2). This violates the owner's requirement of a straight or gently leaning trunk that is never wavy.", "The seed-42 trunk has a distinct kink or lateral jog at mid-upper height (render-1). This violates the owner's never-wavy requirement.", "The trunk surface is a smooth dark cylinder with sparse, isolated domed knobs. Reference-1 and reference-2 show a dense spiral lattice of wedge-shaped leaf-base stubs packed with reddish-brown fibre (render-2, render-3).", "The leaflets render as tiny short flecks along each rachis. The frond does not read as the stiff, plumose, V-sectioned form with a bristly margin seen in reference-0 and reference-1 (render-0, render-1, render-2)."], "observations": ["render-0 (seed 1, P-WHOLE): a single tall, slender trunk with a small basal flare. The upper third is visibly wavy. It carries a small radial crown of about 25–30 thin fronds, and small knobs are scattered along the trunk.", "render-1 (seed 42, P-WHOLE): the same construction, with a pronounced kink at mid-upper trunk height. The crown is again small and made of thin spokes, with only slight droop in the lowest fronds.", "render-2 (seed 1, P-TRUNK): the closer view confirms the fronds are narrow rachises with short leaflets, radiating mostly outward. The trunk curves gently in an S-shape and is dotted with sparse rounded knobs.", "render-3 (seed 1, P-BASE; metadata visibility 'hidden'): a close view of a smooth, uniformly dark cylinder with four or five isolated domed or blunt-cone knobs. There is no lattice, no fibre and no flat angular stub faces.", "Apart from the knob stubs, nothing grows on the trunk in either seed: no branches, foliage, epiphytes or vines. The trunk is single and unbranched, with near-constant diameter above the basal flare.", "Finish floor: at silhouette level the renders are clean and comparable to the spruce anchor (anchor-0). The anchor sets finish quality only; morphology was judged against the references alone.", "No fruit bunches are rendered. The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed.", "Reference-0 shows a leaning, curved trunk. The owner requirement is authoritative that the trunk must never be wavy, so the render's bends are not accepted as reference variation."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown spread is roughly a quarter of trunk height in both seeds, the fronds are thin sparse spokes, and there is no dense rosette. The reference crowns are massive, with long fronds whose length is a large fraction of trunk height.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size are likely set too low. The owner names these as the first dials."}, {"observation": "The lowest fronds barely droop below the crown apex. Most fronds point upward or horizontally, forming a starburst rather than an arching, recurved shuttlecock with a drooping lower tier.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond arch or droop for the older, outer fronds may be too weak, or the fronds may be too short and light to express curvature."}, {"observation": "The leaflets are tiny, short flecks. The frond does not read as a stiff, narrow, plumose V-section with a bristly silhouette.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Leaflet length or size may be undersized."}, {"observation": "The seed-1 trunk has an S-bend in its upper third, and the seed-42 trunk has a sharp mid-height kink. Both are wavy, not straight or gently leaning. Diameter stays near-constant apart from the basal flare.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Trunk path noise or wobble may still be active on the palm stem. Taper is outside the dial table, so diameter is already where the owner wants it."}, {"observation": "The trunk surface shows sparse, isolated rounded knobs on a smooth dark cylinder. There is no dense spiral diamond lattice of wedge stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The fn-110 leaf-base organs may be too sparse and too small, and rounded rather than angular."}, {"observation": "No fibrous matting fills the gaps between stubs. The trunk is uniformly smooth.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Apart from the leaf-base stubs, nothing grows on the trunk in either seed: no branches, foliage or epiphytes.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The stem is a single unbranched column of near-constant diameter in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches are rendered. Reference-0 shows orange bunches, but reference-1 and reference-2 show crown bases without fruit. That makes the inventory's 'core' status for this trait contestable, since fruit may be seasonal.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed."}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render carries metadata visibility 'hidden', yet the supplied image clearly shows the trunk surface close up. The fail rests on what is drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The dead-frond skirt, the orange petiole sheath and trunk colour weathering are absent or simplified. These are secondary refinements.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Epiphytic ferns on the reference trunks are scene features, not species character. Their absence in the render matches the owner's requirement that nothing grow on the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2", "render-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The render crowns are small starbursts of about 25–30 short, thin fronds with minimal droop. They do not form a dense hemisphere or shuttlecock of long arching fronds."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are tiny short flecks. The frond lacks the plumose, V-sectioned, bristly character of the references."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render shows sparse, isolated domed knobs, not a dense spiral lattice of angular wedge stubs."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk surface is smooth and uniform, with no fibre between stubs."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The stem is single, unbranched and of near-constant diameter in both seeds. The waviness defect is scored under the owner's straight-trunk priority."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Fruit is absent from the render because fn-111 has not landed. It is seen only in reference-0, and the fruitless crowns in reference-1 and reference-2 contest its core status, so the trait is reported unknown rather than dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "owner-fronds-long-arching", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds remain far too short and thin, and the lowest fronds do not droop in either seed."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-straight-constant", "status": "fail", "evi